```yaml
spec:
  grid: 14x14, background 0
  output: 3x3 crop showing the winning sprite on background
  sprites:
    count: 3-8 total, forming 2-3 distinct types
    bbox: always 3x3
    cells: 4-6 filled cells per sprite within the 3x3 bbox
    connectivity: 8-connected (many use diagonal-only links, NOT 4-connected)
    monochromatic: each sprite is one non-zero color
    color-type bijection: each color maps to exactly one shape and vice versa [observed]
  type_counts:
    winner: uniquely most frequent type, margin of exactly 1 over runner-up
    distribution_examples: [4,3,1] or [3,2] or [2,1] or [3,2,1]
  placement:
    same-color sprites must not be 8-adjacent (else they merge)
    different-color sprites may be 8-adjacent
    sprites may touch grid edges (bbox can start at row/col 0 or end at 13)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (simple enough; no inversion needed)
  steps:
    1. Choose K=2-3 distinct non-zero colors and for each create a random 3x3 binary mask with 4-6 filled cells that is 8-connected (verify with scipy.ndimage.label)
    2. Assign counts so one type has a unique maximum with margin 1 (e.g. for K=2 pick [N, N-1]; for K=3 pick [N, N-1, M] with M < N)
    3. Place sprites on the 14x14 grid: for each instance pick a random top-left (r,c) in [0..11]x[0..11], stamp the mask, reject if any same-color foreground pixel is 8-adjacent to existing same-color pixels (different colors may touch)
    4. Output is the 3x3 grid with winning type's mask painted in its color on background 0
